Refuses an unqualified target that two packages both declare.

Choosing one would rename the wrong User everywhere, so the message names the
packages it found and both spellings that disambiguate.

-- args --
rename field User.Name Title

-- want.error --
field User.Name is declared in more than one package (example.com/ambiguous/api, example.com/ambiguous/store); qualify the target with the one you mean, as in "example.com/ambiguous/api.User.Name", or with the directory it is in

-- go.mod --
module example.com/ambiguous

go 1.22

-- store/user.in.go --
package store

type User struct {
	Name string
}

-- api/user.in.go --
package api

type User struct {
	Name string
}
